From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anaconda Recipes <recipe-maintainers@anaconda.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Drop -Werror=unused-result from the downloaded TF .bazelrc

configure.sh downloads TF's .bazelrc as the build's main config, and its
common:linux section promotes -Wunused-result to an error.  protobuf 7
marks several APIs [[nodiscard]] (PrintToString, AppendToString,
ParseFromString, ...), and TF/TSL/XLA sources ignore the returns in a
number of places, so every linux build fails during compilation.

Remove the -Werror promotion (keeping -Wunused-result as a warning),
matching the tensorflow-feedstock approach for its own builds.
---
 oss_scripts/configure.sh | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/oss_scripts/configure.sh b/oss_scripts/configure.sh
--- a/oss_scripts/configure.sh
+++ b/oss_scripts/configure.sh
@@ -59,6 +59,9 @@ curl https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tensorflow/tensorflow/v2.21.0/.bazelversi
 curl https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tensorflow/tensorflow/v2.21.0/.bazelrc -o .bazelrc
 # This line breaks Windows builds, so we remove it.
 sed -i -e 's/build --noincompatible_remove_legacy_whole_archive//' .bazelrc
+# protobuf 7 marks APIs [[nodiscard]]; drop -Werror=unused-result so ignored
+# returns in TF/TSL/XLA sources stay warnings on linux.
+sed -i -e 's/ --copt="-Werror=unused-result"//' .bazelrc
 
 write_to_bazelrc "build:manylinux2014 --config=release_cpu_linux"
 write_to_bazelrc "test --test_env=TF_USE_LEGACY_KERAS=1"
